=== CSP Governance Gate — local repro of VALIDATOR-CHECK.yml's exact check ===
$ git diff origin/main -- 'services/gateway/src/frontend/' 'services/gateway/dist/frontend/' > /tmp/csp_diff.txt
$ node scripts/ci/validator-path-guard.cjs --csp-added-lines /tmp/csp_diff.txt

First attempt: REJECTED — CSP_PATTERNS' /\.style\b/ flagged the new badges'
scripted inline-style assignment (`.style.cssText = '...'`), matching this
file's own pervasive pre-existing pattern but tripping the gate on any NEW
addition of it. Fixed by moving the badge styling to a CSS class
(`.llm-provider-badge` in styles.css) and `element.className = '...'`
instead — cleaner anyway, and avoids relitigating the gate's own CSP
semantics. Re-ran after the fix:

No CSP pattern hits in added lines.
exit: 0

(A second false-positive round-trip: the explanatory code comment ITSELF
used the literal substring ".style" and re-tripped the same naive
substring-match gate — the same self-matching failure mode this repo's own
CLAUDE.md changelog already documents for VALIDATOR-CHECK.yml's `<script`/
`unsafe-inline` patterns. Reworded the comment to avoid the literal
substring; not a gate change, just careful wording, since the gate is
shared governance tooling out of scope for this PR.)

